      "timeoriginalestimate": 28800,
      "description": "h3. Overview\n\nImplement subtraction functionality in the calculator application to allow users to subtract one numeric value from another and view the calculated result.\n\nh3. Business Requirement\n\nAs a user of the calculator application, I want to subtract one number from another so that I can quickly calculate the difference between two values.\n\nh3. Functional Requirements\n\nThe calculator should:\n\n# Provide a *Subtraction (-)* operation.\n# Allow the user to enter two numeric operands.\n# Subtract the second operand from the first operand when the subtraction operation is selected.\n# Display the calculated result to the user.\n# Support both positive and negative numbers.\n# Support decimal values.\n# Handle valid zero values correctly.\n# Preserve the order of the operands, ensuring that the second operand is subtracted from the first.\n\nh3. Example Scenarios\n\n||Input 1||Operation||Input 2||Expected Result||\n|10|-|3|7|\n|25|-|10|15|\n|3|-|5|-2|\n|-5|-|-3|-2|\n|5.5|-|2.5|3|\n|10|-|0|10|\n|0|-|10|-10|\n|0|-|0|0|\n\nh2. Acceptance Criteria\n\nh3. AC1 — Subtraction of Positive Numbers\n\n*Given* the user has entered two positive numbers\n*When* the user selects the subtraction operation\n*Then* the calculator should subtract the second number from the first and display the correct result.\n\nh3. AC2 — Negative Result\n\n*Given* the first operand is smaller than the second operand\n*When* the user performs a subtraction operation\n*Then* the calculator should correctly calculate and display the resulting negative value.\n\nh3. AC3 — Subtraction of Negative Numbers\n\n*Given* the user has entered one or more negative numbers\n*When* the user performs a subtraction operation\n*Then* the calculator should correctly calculate and display the resulting value.\n\nh3. AC4 — Subtraction of Decimal Numbers\n\n*Given* the user has entered one or more decimal values\n*When* the user performs a subtraction operation\n*Then* the calculator should correctly calculate and display the decimal result.\n\nh3. AC5 — Subtraction Involving Zero\n\n*Given* one or both operands are zero\n*When* the user performs a subtraction operation\n*Then* the calculator should correctly return the difference without errors.\n\nh3. AC6 — Operand Order\n\n*Given* the user has entered two valid operands\n*When* the user performs a subtraction operation\n*Then* the calculator should subtract the second operand from the first operand.\n\nFor example, {{10 - 4}} must produce {{6}}, while {{4 - 10}} must produce {{-6}}.\n\nh3. AC7 — Result Display\n\n*Given* a valid subtraction operation has been performed\n*When* the calculation completes\n*Then* the calculated result should be clearly displayed in the calculator interface.\n\nh3. AC8 — Invalid Input Handling\n\n*Given* the user provides an invalid or incomplete input for the subtraction operation\n*When* the user attempts to perform the calculation\n*Then* the application should prevent an invalid calculation and provide appropriate feedback or maintain the current valid calculator state.\n\nh3. AC9 — Regression\n\n*Given* the subtraction functionality has been implemented\n*When* the existing calculator functionality is used\n*Then* existing operations and functionality should continue to work as expected without regression.\n\nh2. Technical Notes\n\n* Implement the subtraction operation following the existing architecture and coding conventions of the calculator application.\n* Keep the subtraction logic isolated and testable.\n* Add appropriate unit tests covering positive, negative, decimal, zero-value, and operand-order scenarios.\n* Ensure the implementation does not introduce regressions to existing calculator operations.\n\nh2. Definition of Done\n\n* Subtraction operation is implemented.\n* Subtraction is accessible through the calculator UI.\n* Positive, negative, decimal, and zero-value scenarios are supported.\n* Operand order is correctly maintained.\n* Appropriate error handling is implemented for invalid/incomplete input.\n* Unit tests have been added and are passing.\n* Existing calculator functionality continues to work.\n* Code follows the project's established coding standards.\n* Changes have been reviewed and are ready for merge.",
